    "explanation": "Privacy: The right to privacy encompasses the ability to control access to personal information and spaces. An unauthorized search into a citizen's residence directly infringes on this right by invading their personal domain without due process. Freedom of conscience: While an unwarranted search might invade some aspects of personal beliefs, it wouldn't directly infringe on the freedom to hold and practice one's own beliefs. Freedom of expression: This fundamental right is concerned with expressing oneself publicly, not necessarily within the private space of one's residence. An illegal search wouldn't directly suppress or control public expression. Life: While a violation of privacy can have serious consequences, it wouldn't directly threaten the right to life, which is the most fundamental human right."
